  "title": "Vowel signs 2: ু ূ ৃ",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "These three signs hang **below** the consonant.\n\n**ু** and **ূ** both say `u` (as in *food*): ফুফু (`fufu`), খালু (`khalu`), আপু (`apu`), দুধ (`dudh`, *milk*), দূরে (`dure`, *far*), পূজা (`puja`). Like ি/ী they **sound the same**; only the spelling differs. The long-u sign ূ has an extra loop.\n\n**Shape changes**: after a few letters the sign joins in a new way. In **রু** and **রূ** the sign sits on the right side of র instead of underneath; in **হু** and **হৃ** it becomes a curl or hook under হ; in **শু** and **গু** it folds into the letter. When a shape looks new, find the base letter first, then the sign.\n\n**ৃ** is the sign form of ঋ and says `ri`: কৃষক (`krishok`, *farmer*), পৃথিবী (`prithibi`, *world*). Don't mix up কৃ (`kri`) with কু (`ku`): ৃ is a small hook, ু a loop.",
  "vocab": [
    {
      "id": "k-u",
      "bn": "কু",
      "tr": "ku",
      "en": "ু (u-kar, short-u sign): adds 'u' as in 'food'",
      "notes": "Bare sign: ু (U+09C1), name hroshsho u-kar (হ্রস্ব উ-কার). Below the letter; joins differently after র, হ, শ, গ (রু, হু, শু, গু). Same sound as ূ."
    },
    {
      "id": "k-uu",
      "bn": "কূ",
      "tr": "ku",
      "en": "ূ (long-u sign): adds 'u' as in 'food'",
      "notes": "Bare sign: ূ (U+09C2), name dirgho u-kar (দীর্ঘ উ-কার). Same sound as ু. After র it becomes রূ."
    },
    {
      "id": "k-ri",
      "bn": "কৃ",
